Venetium 0069 - feature level 9_x: no depth textures (WebGL pages that sample one drew nothing).
1. With v1.3.1.2 on the Lumia 735, webglsamples.org/field showed only its blue clear color. Reproduced on WARP at 9_3
   with the x86 build running the ARM32 9_3 paths (0065, 0067; test-only switches, not in this patch): every frame
   logged "Error allocating ShaderResourceView" (HRESULT 0x80070057), and a test-only probe showed the view: format
   UNKNOWN on a 1024x1024 D24_UNORM_S8_UINT texture bound only as a depth-stencil target.
2. At 9_x ANGLE's format table gives the depth formats no shader resource view format (srvFormat UNKNOWN below 10_0:
   a 9_x device cannot sample depth), but GenerateTextureFormatCaps still counts them texturable (a depth-stencil
   Texture2D can be created), so GL_ANGLE_depth_texture, and with it WEBGL_depth_texture, was offered. The field
   sample renders its scene depth into one and samples it for depth of field; that draw failed every frame. At 9_x
   the extension is no longer offered (0067's 9_x block), so pages take their fallback: the field sample then encodes
   depth in alpha and draws correctly on WARP at 9_3, with no errors. A sweep of every other WebGL texture format at
   9_3 (upload, nearest / linear / mipmapped sampling, render target) found nothing else that fails. _M_ARM only.

diff --git a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/d3d11/renderer11_utils.cpp b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/d3d11/renderer11_utils.cpp
--- a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/d3d11/renderer11_utils.cpp
+++ b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/d3d11/renderer11_utils.cpp
@@ -1678,6 +1678,12 @@
         extensions->blendFuncExtendedEXT = false;
         caps->maxDualSourceDrawBuffers   = 0;
         extensions->depthClampEXT        = false;
+        // Venetium 0069: and no depth textures. At 9_x the depth formats have no shader resource view format
+        // (texture_format_table: srvFormat UNKNOWN below 10_0), but they still count as texturable, so ANGLE offered
+        // GL_ANGLE_depth_texture (WEBGL_depth_texture): rendering to one worked and every draw that sampled it
+        // failed with "Error allocating ShaderResourceView" (E_INVALIDARG). The WebGL field sample took that path
+        // and drew nothing; without the extension it encodes depth in alpha.
+        extensions->depthTextureANGLE    = false;
     }
 #endif
 
